#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183865 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f458c61-bc51-5653-9ecb-1e96eb5c335e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Limit of an Inverse Trigonometric Function at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "563087c2-8d87-5b95-833d-f9892d9276a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-10535" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 0} \\dfrac{\\arccos(x) -\\pi}{x-\\pi}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\arccos(x){:}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3811/Source/Images/a466fdfbf193e117a9c5e416ee47ffff.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\arccos(x)$ is $x \\in [-1,1]$.\n\nNow, substituting $x=0$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → 0)((\\arccos (x) - π)/(x - π)) &= (\\arccos (0) - π)/(0 - π) \\\\\n&= ((\\frac{π}{2} - π))/((- π)) \\\\\n&= ((-\\frac{π}{2}))/((- π)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183866 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcc5d54-e7fd-5be5-9d00-4240d03e21cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Limits at Infinity"}] :question/id #uuid "c1ba0b9f-78d6-5791-8816-b71da089e57f" :question/math-academy-id "e-10536" :question/problem "What is the value of $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\, \\infty} \\arccos(x-1)$?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of\n\n$$\ny = \\arccos(x-1){:}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3811/Source/Images/0c8e05c838e67b1eaca00925fab12e20.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\arccos(x-1)$ is $x \\in [0,2]$. This means that $\\arccos(x-1)$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\, \\infty} \\arccos(x-1)$ is undefined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183867 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Limit Involving Trigonometric Functions and Their Inverses"}] :question/id #uuid "7ce46ca9-cfff-5e8b-89b9-a2a7b34921fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-10537" :question/problem "Compute the value of $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\, \\infty}\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\arctan \\left(2x+1\\right)\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of\n\n$$\ny =\\arctan \\left(2x+1\\right){:}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3811/Source/Images/3e8fb5c89782322156fbf09f33393408.png)\n\nThe domain of\n\n$$\n\\arctan \\left(2x+1 \\right)\n$$\n\nis $(-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nAs $x$ increases to $\\infty$, the graph tends to\n\n$$\ny={\\color{blue}\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → ∞)\\cos (\\frac{2}{3}\\arctan (2x + 1)) &= \\cos (\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot (\\frac{π}{2})) \\\\\n&= \\cos (\\frac{π}{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a58f115-f368-5171-af73-37084085b42a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Limit Involving Trigonometric Functions and Their Inverses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd1e50c5-17fd-54ac-b5e9-5272c6c9f1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∞" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181209} {:answer/id #uuid "102902b1-548b-5d51-b2da-f0a9a049550f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181210} {:answer/id #uuid "2ade5223-3c88-566d-8688-d20828e0d736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181211} {:answer/id #uuid "62733b1f-741b-56cd-ab26-ba7562c7f90b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181212} {:answer/id #uuid "652b0975-5b45-5ba0-87d7-092747c2da4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ade5223-3c88-566d-8688-d20828e0d736" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181211} :answer-field/id #uuid "36265b7b-d7ba-500f-b44d-b2d731abc742" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181208}] :question/id #uuid "53588a2b-ad7c-5261-a3ca-c56ccdc03a42" :question/math-academy-id "q-149958" :question/problem "What is $lim_(x → - 1/2)\\tan (\\frac{1}{2}\\arccos (x))$?"}]}
